Subject: [PATCH] Consumables preview fix, on-level board guarantee,
 success-rate revert

- QuestCard/sort-by-success/pickBestQuest now pass a hero's actual
  equipped consumables into previewSuccess (were hardcoded to []) --
  the card display and Quick-assign scoring never reflected equipped
  potions, even though real resolution always did.
- New guaranteed on-level offer in generateContractsForHero: forces
  slot 0 to the hero's own at-level tier if none of the 6 generated
  offers qualifies. Verified 0 misses across 18,000 sampled
  generations, levels 1-6 -- but also confirmed this mostly overlaps
  with the existing burst guarantee below level 16, and does NOT fix
  the actual reported symptom (mid-window depletion after burning
  through a board's Easy-tier slots). Flagged as a real follow-up,
  not solved this pass.
- Reverted DIFFICULTIES.baseSuccess (Normal 58->60, Hard 44->50,
  Epic 30->40, Legendary 18->30; Easy untouched, was never part of
  either pass) and guild_facility.barracks/renown_perk.renowned_skill
  successPerLevel (both 1->3) back toward pre-rebalance values, per
  direct request. weapons_training/mounted_travel and the diminishing
  investment curve deliberately NOT reverted -- those fixed a
  separate, still-valid bug from an earlier, distinct request.
- Root-caused why a lightly-injured hero swings success so hard:
  curveInvestment only diminishes positive investment above its
  threshold; injury/health penalties are negative and pass through
  fully uncurved. Documented, not fixed -- deferred per direct
  request to tune injuries separately later.
- guild-idler-status.md updated with full writeup, before/after
  numbers, and the Briar repro confirming the revert does NOT change
  her specific case (injury-driven, not baseSuccess-driven).

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and vite build both clean; 18,000-sample
on-level guarantee test (with and without the fix); zero-investment
and upgrades-maxed success stress tests; Briar's exact injury
scenario reproduced (48.5% vs the reported 49%, confirming no change).
